<title>USA: N.J. announces management group for $2.8 bln deal.</title>
<headline>N.J. announces management group for $2.8 bln deal.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW JERSEY ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $2,750,000,000</p>
<p>STATE PENSION FUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1997A-1997H</p>
<p>(FEDERALLY TAXABLE)</p>
<p>THE STATE OF NEW JERSEY</p>
<p>THE STATE OF NEW JERSEY HAS OFFICIALLY ANNOUNCED THE</p>
<p>MANAGEMENT GROUP FOR ITS UPCOMING PENSION FUNDING BONDS.</p>
<p>THE GROUP IS AS FOLLOWS:</p>
<p>MERRILL LYNCH &amp; CO.</p>
<p>GOLDMAN, SACHS &amp; CO.</p>
<p>LEHMAN BROTHERS</p>
<p>MORGAN STANLEY DEAN WITTER</p>
<p>SMITH BARNEY INC.</p>
<p>DILLON, READ &amp; CO.</p>
<p>COMMERCE CAPITAL, A DIVISION OF COMMERCE BANK</p>
<p>LLAMA COMPANY</p>
<p>WILLIAM E. SIMON &amp; SONS MUNICIPAL SECURITIES INC.</p>
<p>PAINEWEBBER INCORPORATED</p>
<p>BEAR, STEARNS &amp; CO. INC.</p>
<p>FIRST ALBANY CORPORATION</p>
<p>M.R. BEAL &amp; COMPANY</p>
<p>POWELL CAPITAL MARKETS, INC.</p>
<p>GIBRALTAR SECURITIES CO.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter</p>
<p>Smith Barney Inc.</p>
<p>Dillon, Read &amp; Co. Inc.</p>
<p>Commerce Capital, A Division of Commerce Bank.</p>
<p>Llama Company</p>
<p>William E. Simon &amp; Sons Municipal Securities Inc.</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. Inc.</p>
<p>First Albany Corporation</p>
<p>M.R. Beal &amp; Company</p>
<p>Powell Capital Markets, Inc.</p>
<p>Gibraltar Securities Co.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
